    "blocks": [
      {
        "index": 0,
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "section_index": null,
        "text": "The shaft entrance into Cueva Coquisera, 0039 ."
      },
      {
        "index": 1,
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "section_index": null,
        "text": "The following description comes from pp20-21 of the report of the 2025 Campaign by the Colectivo Piezo, linked below."
      },
      {
        "index": 2,
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "section_index": null,
        "text": "As the second entrance to Codisera, it is relatively little known. It consists of a 42m shaft, divided into two sections of ramps containing loose rocks. Shortly into the descent, several high openings can be seen letting in daylight—perhaps where its name comes from."
      },
      {
        "index": 3,
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "section_index": null,
        "text": "At the bottom, we found the access point that reaches the white flowstone of the '400 Pesetas Passage.' A small but constant flow of water feeds this formation. From the other section, after a small 3m drop, you enter a high, narrow, and highly polished meander, which provides access to the intermittent lake in the '400 Pesetas Passage.'"
      },
      {
        "index": 4,
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "section_index": null,
        "text": "There is a photo looking up the shaft on page 21."
      }
    ],
